        <div class="entry-header">
          <h2 class="entry-title">Back to the Drawing Board</h2>
          <p class="entry-meta">category: life/meta</p>
          <p class="entry-meta">date: 7th June 2026, Morning.</p>
          <p class="entry-intro">I have plans that I cannot share right now because the haters are gonna try and sabotage me.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="qa-block">
          <div class="qa-answer">
            <p>Hello, my dearest readers! Short post, but let’s go do some awesome blog post writing :)</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="qa-block">
          <h3 class="qa-question">Life is good!</h3>
          <div class="photo-pair-row">
            <img src="../blogimg/lifeGoodCamera01.jpeg" alt="Taking a photo outside" loading="lazy">
            <img src="../blogimg/lifeGoodCamera02.jpeg" alt="Taking a photo outside" loading="lazy">
          </div>
          <div class="qa-answer">
            <p>A lot of wonderful life has been going on lately :) These past 2 weeks in particular I spent seeing the new Micheal movie with DA FAM™ (which was GAS), backrooms with my Natasha Dearest (which was ALSO GAS OH MY GOD more on this later too) Venturing to IKEA, open mic’ing at The Cup, and celebrating a particular someone’s birthday :)</p>
          </div>
          <div class="photo-trio-row">
            <img src="../blogimg/lifeGoodFriends01.png" alt="Friends at The Cup" loading="lazy">
            <img src="../blogimg/lifeGoodFriends02.png" alt="Two friends outside" loading="lazy">
            <img src="../blogimg/lifeGoodFriends03.png" alt="Friends at a table" loading="lazy">
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="qa-block">
          <h3 class="qa-question">Sabbatical to Bangkok</h3>
          <img class="entry-media framed" src="../blogimg/backroomsBangkok.jpg" alt="Luca standing in front of a colorful mural" loading="lazy">
          <div class="qa-answer">
            <p>Major update: I’m gonna release blog posts a hair less often for the time being, kinda on a sporadic when-I-feel kinda schedule! Truth be told, this might even end up meaning I write more often in a bit, but a little break is in order at least.</p>
            <p>I’m back in the planning/writing phase of my cycle, which means I don’t have a whole lot to talk about on the music front. It’s been hard to pump out a huge amount of content because of this on the blog, but I will say that something I’m learning to appreciate the ‘downtime’ in downtime!</p>
            <p>It’s nice to know that there can be quiet peaceful moments of chill relaxation and routine, outside of the exciting action-packed weekends we spend releasing albums and going crazy. This Sunday, for instance, I have <i>no</i> plans. It’s a good break.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="qa-block">
          <h3 class="qa-question">Here’s What I’m Looking Forward to:</h3>
          <div class="qa-answer">
            <p>I’m almost 23 years old! My debut album 521 is almost five whole years old. Both of these are insane to me. I’m working on a special 5-year anniversary edition release of 521, that will include a second ‘disc’ worth of extras like unreleased songs!</p>
            <p>There are a lot of songs I wrote in the 2021-2022 era that I don’t really feel represent the era of musicianship I’m in right now, and because of that I haven’t put them out. I still recorded them professionally, though, and like them for what they are. I’m of the opinion that putting them on this deluxe album gives them a proper home where they can live.</p>
            <p>It’s gonna be fun to revisit what made me me at the time, and I’m looking forward to you guys hearing the songs that didn’t make the cut!</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="qa-block">
          <h3 class="qa-question">Finally,</h3>
          <div class="qa-answer">
            <p>Last announcements: The Kiss and Tell Show has a <a href="https://lucadigrigoli.bandcamp.com/album/the-kiss-and-tell-show">cd now!</a> if that’s something you’re interested in. I’m looking into making more cool merch, because this album is really fun to promote and make stuff for.</p>
            <p>The next full-length album is in the works. It won’t take five years this time, promise.</p>
            <p>You guys are awesome. Y’all reading my blog here means a lot to me, and there’s more of it to come. I will be spending some time playing Stardew, open mic’ing, turning 23, and more!</p>
            <p>I will keep you updated here, on a more-or-less weekly basis but likely less for a little bit, and we shall keep doing this awesome thing we do!</p>
            <p><i>~Luca</i></p>
          </div>
